{"kind":"artifact","text":"AGENTS.md at head 85e5dbb2: the quiet-wave precondition now fails closed on a refused report.\n\nReview proved the old form fail-open from the live log, not in principle. It recognised a verdict by filtering projection.statements for kind \"report\" with an approved or changes-requested body — but statements includes reports the fold refused, so a malformed or unauthorized report could settle a review it had no standing to settle. Three such reports are live today. It also keyed settlement by artifact name, so one chain's verdict settled every other request naming the same artifact. Together they hid five review requests that no effective verdict binds.\n\nThe check now reads projection.reviews, which the fold populates only from effective reports, and binds settlement to the request event through projection.commitments. The approved-head check reads the head from the review record, which carries the exact commit the verdict was signed over.\n\nWorth stating plainly because it nearly escaped: both forms report 20 awaiting. The old number was not visibly wrong, because it counted artifact-name occurrences while the new one counts requests. Agreement between two different denominators is not agreement, and I would have taken it as confirmation if I had not gone looking for the disagreement request by request.\n\nThis retires five predecessors at this exact path, all mine. Four of them should have been retired when their successors were published; only the fifth is this head's own predecessor. A path can hold one live artifact, and this one was holding five.\n\n`go vet ./...` clean; both jq blocks verified by running them exactly as written against the current projection.","body":{"commit":"85e5dbb2b0137b4c02f4098b2a6ba0ea5ee50d9e","path":"AGENTS.md"}}